{"questions":[{"question_id":"cIb7tW44TFvHbqdR","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2002","year":2002,"examDate":2002,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"quantitative-measures-in-chemical-equations","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"in-a-compound-c-h-and-n-atoms-are-present-in-9-1-35-y-weight-jee-main-2002-marks-4-cib7tw44tfvhbqdr.htm","content":"In a compound C, H and N atoms are present in 9 : 1 : 3.5 by weight . Molecular weight of the compound is 108 g mol<sup>-1</sup> . Molecular formula of compound is","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub>N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>4</sub>N"},{"identifier":"C","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>8</sub>N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"C<sub>9</sub>H<sub>12</sub>N<sub>3</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<table class=\"tg\">\n  <tbody><tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\">Element</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\">Weight ratio</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\">No of atoms of element</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\">Simplest Ratio</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-amwm\">C</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">9</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">9/12 = 3/4</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">3</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-amwm\">H</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">1</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">1/1 = 1</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">4</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-amwm\">N</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">3.5</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">3.5/14 = 1/4</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">1</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<br>\nEmpherical Formula of the compound (EF) will be <b>C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>4</sub>N</b><br><br>\nNow to find molecular formula at first find number of moles of given mass<br><br>\nNo. of moles (n) = <span style=\"display: inline-block;vertical-align: middle;\">\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;border-bottom: 1px solid black;\">Given mass</div>\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;\">Molar mass</div>\n</span><br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.054ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.242ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -525 1000 549\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21D2\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21D2\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.816ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.395ex\" height=\"2.773ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 1500.7 1225.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(396.8,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1260.7\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> <br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.054ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.242ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -525 1000 549\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21D2\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21D2\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 2 <br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>  No. of Moles is 2<br><br>\nMolecular formula (MF) = n (no. of moles) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Empherical Formula (EF)<br> <br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.054ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.242ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -525 1000 549\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21D2\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-T